course: dictionary
lesson: 7358
title: Playtime and school breaks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Playtime is a time for playing. At school it is the short break when children go outside. Clues in the sentence tell you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Jayden forgot his homework, did it at lunch and missed playtime.» Jayden had to use his break to finish his work, so playtime must be the time he could have spent playing outside.
explain: Playtime does not only happen at school. «It's playtime for the puppy!» means it is time for the puppy to play. Phrases help too: at playtime, after playtime, playtime is over, and wet playtime, which means indoor play when it rains.
fact: Playtime means a time for playing, especially the break at school when children go outside.
fact: Playtime can also be a set time for a child or a pet to play.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, playtime is the short break at school.
fact: In the USA, the same break is called «recess».
fact: «Wet playtime» means indoor play when it rains.
exercise: «He did it at lunch and missed playtime.» What is playtime in this sentence? | A bedtime story | A lesson about sport | *The short break at school when children go outside | A long holiday from school
exercise: «It's playtime for the puppy!» What does playtime mean here? | A visit to the vet | A walk to the shop | *A set time for the puppy to play | A time for the puppy to sleep
exercise: Ben's class has a wet playtime today. What is a wet playtime? | A puddle race outside | A swimming lesson | *Indoor play because it is raining | A quiet sleep after lunch
test: In «"perERva" means break or playtime», what does perERva mean? | Hometime | Lesson | Homework | *Break or playtime
test: «Playtime is over» means that: | The children are playing a game | The break is about to begin | Everyone is going home now | *The break has ended and lessons start again
exam: «Dan lost his playtime» after answering back to the dinner lady. What does this mean? | *He had to miss his break outside as a punishment | He won an extra game at break | He was sent home early | He was given a new playground
